    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nSelecting `load_workloads(container_tag=\"fixture\", environment=\"dev\", tag=\"latest\")` against the complete recipe set raises `KeyError: 'tag'` on a functional workload instead of selecting the tagged unit-test workloads.\n\nThe optional-field guards use `hasattr(dotdict(...), field)`, but `dotdict.__getattr__ = dict.get` returns `None` for missing fields, so `hasattr` always succeeds. Use dictionary lookup with a default for tag, environment, and platform filtering.\n\nThe regressions exercise the full current recipe set and all three production filters with matching, nonmatching, and missing fields.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Reproduced on unchanged production code: focused regressions **4 failed**.\n- After the fix, the same focused tests **4 passed** in the Linux Python 3.12 CPU tooling container.\n- `uv run --no-project --python /opt/cpu-review/bin/python isort` on both changed files; Black 26 check, isort check, Ruff, and Python compile checks passed.\n- Required `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` completed successfully with the pinned Black 26.3.0, isort 5.13.2, Pylint 3.2.6, and Ruff 0.9.10. Its nonblocking mypy step reports 18 pre-existing source errors, confirmed on unchanged baseline; no new mypy diagnostics.\n- GPU training validation is not covered by these CPU orchestration tests.\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest -q tests/test_utils/python_scripts/test_recipe_optional_filters.py\n```\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: none; this is a small, reproduced bug fix, not a new feature or GPU kernel.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] Added relevant focused regressions.\n- [ ] Added GPU functional tests.\n- [x] Ran the repository formatter.\n\nAI-assisted draft; human author review and NVIDIA GPU/full CI validation are pending. The personal author-review checkbox is left unchecked.\n",
